      "notes": "All claims are adequately supported by their cited evidence. The stated-tier claim accurately reflects the policy text. The 4% household figure (E4) is from commercial/media sources but is corroborated by E5 and E6, and is used conservatively. The E22/E23 quotes from Resolution Foundation (advocacy/institutional) support the regressive-baseline claims without overstating them. The E24 claim is correctly tiered as projected and explicitly distinguished from the policy under review. Tier integrity is maintained throughout. The direction of 'worsens' is evidence-led: the concrete beneficiary population is wealthier-skewed solar owners, and no funded low-income mechanism is in the stated text. The rationale attributes no motive or party identity. Magnitude 'minor' is justified by the small affected population. No false balance issue: the verdict does not claim mixed/too-uncertain, and the one potential countervailing channel (low-income provisions) is correctly identified as absent from the stated text. One minor note: E4's sources (greenenergyelectrical.com, sunsave.energy) are commercial, but the claim is used directionally and is consistent with E5/E6, so not blocking."
